  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The controversy follows a match where PSS Sleman suffered a 3-0 loss to Arema FC in the BRI Super League. Following the defeat, spectators engaged in unrest, which included the burning of goal netting at the stadium. This incident has drawn international attention, with PSSI chairman Erick Thohir confirming that FIFA has contacted the federation to inquire about the security breach. In response to the unrest, PSSI has indicated that it is cooperating with national police to investigate the events and is weighing significant sanctions against PSS Sleman. Options under review for the club include point deductions. Prior to this match, PSS Sleman had been undergoing intensive training under a temporary coach to prepare for league competition during the FIFA break. Club representatives have acknowledged that the team struggled with focus during the performance that preceded the stadium disturbance.",
